   "text": "I did not derive every stereocentre from the wedges and hashes. I assembled this SMILES from the connectivity in the drawing, taking the stereodescriptors from my recollection of bleomycin's isomeric SMILES, so the stereo marks are unverified.\n\nThe structure reads as a bleomycin-type glycopeptide with an agmatine tail:\n\n- **Left end:** a guanidine, N=C(N)N, joined through a four-carbon chain and an amide NH to a bithiazole.\n- **Middle:** a threonine unit, then a hydroxy-methylpentanoic acid unit (the 3-hydroxy-2,4-dimethyl-5-aminopentanoyl residue). Next comes a \u03b2-hydroxyhistidine unit carrying a disaccharide, a gulose with a mannose bearing a carbamate, attached through an ether oxygen.\n- **Right end:** a 5-methyl-4-amino pyrimidine bearing the side chain with the secondary amine and two primary amide groups.\n\nI checked the sugar order against the image. The gulose, with its CH2OH, sits on the histidine oxygen, and the carbamoyl mannose is attached to the gulose.\n\nSMILES: CC1=C(N=C(N=C1N)[C@H](CC(=O)N)NC[C@@H](C(=O)N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@H](C2=CN=CN2)O[C@H]3[C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](O3)CO)O)O)O[C@@H]4[C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O4)CO)O)OC(=O)N)O)C(=O)N[C@H](C)[C@H]([C@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)NCCC5=NC(=CS5)C6=NC(=CS6)C(=O)NCCCCN=C(N)N)O"
